# Task-pipeline: commit before done

On the **commit** phase status stays `in-progress` (phase `commit`) until `git commit` succeeds.

## Order

1. Remote / checks / Docker cleanup — still while `in-progress`/`commit`.
2. Prepare changes → `TP set … --status done --phase done` (task rename) → `git add` (including rename) → one `git commit`.
3. Push (`push: true`) after a successful commit. Push failure does not undo `done`.

## Rollback

If `git commit` failed after `set done`: immediately `TP set … --status in-progress --phase commit --force`, describe the failure in `fix-plan.md`, do not treat the task as closed.
